WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:03.136
The FBI is harshly criticized

00:00:03.136 --> 00:00:04.804
in a new long awaited report

00:00:04.804 --> 00:00:05.638
on the origins

00:00:05.638 --> 00:00:07.407
of the Trump-Russia investigation.

00:00:07.407 --> 00:00:08.541
The veteran prosecutor, Don

00:00:08.541 --> 00:00:10.076
Durham, says the agency ignored

00:00:10.076 --> 00:00:11.644
its own rules and procedures

00:00:11.644 --> 00:00:13.680
and was way too quick to take a tip

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:15.548
about the 2016 Trump campaign

00:00:15.548 --> 00:00:16.449
and accelerated

00:00:16.449 --> 00:00:18.184
into a full blown investigation

00:00:18.184 --> 00:00:19.919
of whether there was communication

00:00:19.919 --> 00:00:21.721
or collusion with Russia.

00:00:21.721 --> 00:00:23.123
But Durham proposed

00:00:23.123 --> 00:00:24.391
no new charges

00:00:24.391 --> 00:00:25.892
and only modest FBI

00:00:25.892 --> 00:00:27.660
reforms in his final report

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:28.495
and his findings,

00:00:28.495 --> 00:00:30.530
while harshly critical of the FBI,

00:00:30.697 --> 00:00:31.197
come nowhere

00:00:31.197 --> 00:00:33.033
close to how they're now being portrayed

00:00:33.033 --> 00:00:34.167
by the former president

00:00:34.167 --> 00:00:35.535
and some of his allies.

00:00:35.535 --> 00:00:36.336
Let's get some insights

00:00:36.336 --> 00:00:37.537
now from CNN's Evan Perez

00:00:37.537 --> 00:00:39.005
and the former federal prosecutor,

00:00:39.005 --> 00:00:39.706
Elliott Williams.

00:00:39.706 --> 00:00:42.175
It is a damning report from Mr.

00:00:42.175 --> 00:00:42.909
Durham, essentially

00:00:42.909 --> 00:00:44.844
saying that they got this tip

00:00:44.844 --> 00:00:46.379
and they should have taken their time

00:00:46.379 --> 00:00:47.113
and explored it.

00:00:47.113 --> 00:00:47.814
And instead,

00:00:47.814 --> 00:00:48.782
because of what he sees

00:00:48.782 --> 00:00:50.617
as a predisposition against Trump,

00:00:50.617 --> 00:00:51.885
they rushed into a full blown

00:00:51.885 --> 00:00:52.452
investigation,

00:00:52.452 --> 00:00:53.686
which gives them a lot more power.

00:00:53.686 --> 00:00:54.721
They can do a lot more things.

00:00:54.721 --> 00:00:55.722
He said they used raw

00:00:55.722 --> 00:00:56.423
and analyzed

00:00:56.423 --> 00:00:58.024
and uncorroborated intelligence.

00:00:58.024 --> 00:00:59.626
He believes some personnel involved

00:00:59.626 --> 00:01:01.394
had a predisposition against Trump,

00:01:01.394 --> 00:01:03.296
that there was no evidence of collusion.

00:01:03.296 --> 00:01:04.831
But he doesn't recommend

00:01:04.831 --> 00:01:05.932
wholesale new charges

00:01:05.932 --> 00:01:07.667
or any wholesale changes.

00:01:07.667 --> 00:01:09.602
So essentially, since they screwed up.

00:01:09.602 --> 00:01:12.005
Right. But it's not a giant problem.

00:01:12.005 --> 00:01:12.705
Is that fair?

00:01:12.705 --> 00:01:14.707
Well, I mean, look, it is a big problem

00:01:15.008 --> 00:01:17.143
that the FBI made a lot of the mistakes

00:01:17.143 --> 00:01:19.045
that were documented in this report.

00:01:19.045 --> 00:01:21.314
The problem for for Durham

00:01:21.314 --> 00:01:23.116
is that he was brought in

00:01:23.116 --> 00:01:25.452
after a very, very exhaustive

00:01:25.718 --> 00:01:27.287
inspector general report, found

00:01:27.287 --> 00:01:28.054
pretty much everything

00:01:28.054 --> 00:01:30.390
he just described in 2019.

00:01:31.257 --> 00:01:32.559
He was appointed

00:01:32.559 --> 00:01:34.394
because the former president

00:01:34.394 --> 00:01:34.928
was obsessed

00:01:34.928 --> 00:01:36.563
with this idea that he was spied on

00:01:36.563 --> 00:01:37.831
that there was a

00:01:37.831 --> 00:01:39.432
that there was a deep state cabal

00:01:39.432 --> 00:01:41.167
that was out to get him.

00:01:41.167 --> 00:01:42.435
There was all of these things

00:01:42.435 --> 00:01:44.504
that that were promised that,

00:01:44.504 --> 00:01:45.705
you know, Durham himself,

00:01:45.705 --> 00:01:46.106
you know

00:01:46.106 --> 00:01:47.340
raised expectations

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:48.741
of what he was going to find.

00:01:48.741 --> 00:01:51.044
And none of that panned out in the end.

00:01:51.044 --> 00:01:52.712
What Durham found is that, you know,

00:01:52.712 --> 00:01:54.114
these are human beings.

00:01:54.114 --> 00:01:55.048
There were very,

00:01:55.048 --> 00:01:56.950
very extraordinary circumstances.

00:01:56.950 --> 00:01:59.552
You had a candidate. Right.

00:01:59.552 --> 00:02:00.653
Who was being shunned

00:02:00.653 --> 00:02:01.788
by the establishment.

00:02:01.788 --> 00:02:02.755
So he brought in

00:02:02.755 --> 00:02:04.791
a lot of these third rate people,

00:02:04.791 --> 00:02:06.392
some of whom had,

00:02:06.426 --> 00:02:07.193
you know, issues

00:02:07.193 --> 00:02:08.394
and connections in Russia.

00:02:08.394 --> 00:02:11.364
And so that is partly what drove the FBI.

00:02:11.397 --> 00:02:12.932
They made a lot of mistakes.

00:02:12.932 --> 00:02:14.701
But it appears, according to Durham,

00:02:14.701 --> 00:02:16.369
it wasn't a political bias.

00:02:16.369 --> 00:02:17.971
It was simply confirmation bias.

00:02:17.971 --> 00:02:18.371
It was

00:02:18.471 --> 00:02:19.772
it was what prosecutors

00:02:19.772 --> 00:02:21.875
and sometimes what FBI agents do

00:02:21.875 --> 00:02:22.876
at the beginning of this.

00:02:22.876 --> 00:02:23.343
It might be hard

00:02:23.343 --> 00:02:24.344
because this is for years,

00:02:24.344 --> 00:02:24.978
it might be hard for people

00:02:24.978 --> 00:02:25.879
to remember the origins.

00:02:25.879 --> 00:02:26.579
Trump Attorney

00:02:26.579 --> 00:02:27.480
General Bill Barr

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:29.249
asked John Durham, a veteran prosecutor,

00:02:29.249 --> 00:02:30.583
to look into this way back

00:02:30.583 --> 00:02:31.651
then at the beginning.

00:02:31.651 --> 00:02:33.153
This is Trump on the Hugh Hewitt Show.

00:02:33.153 --> 00:02:35.221
So he believe this is going to be huge.

00:02:37.524 --> 00:02:38.091
I think you're going to

00:02:38.091 --> 00:02:39.492
have a very interesting report

00:02:39.492 --> 00:02:40.760
coming out with Durham.

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:42.695
I believe it's bigger

00:02:42.695 --> 00:02:44.797
and far more far reaching

00:02:44.797 --> 00:02:47.000
and far more powerful

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:49.969
than anyone ever thought possible.

00:02:49.969 --> 00:02:51.404
Now, Donald

00:02:51.404 --> 00:02:52.539
Trump, a candidate for president

00:02:52.539 --> 00:02:54.474
again, was very quick to rush out a fund

00:02:54.474 --> 00:02:55.875
fundraising email with the headline.

00:02:55.875 --> 00:02:57.944
I was framed it goes on to say,

00:02:57.944 --> 00:02:58.478
This is horrible.

00:02:58.478 --> 00:03:01.080
It was not that he is exaggerating

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:02.315
what Mr. Durham found.

00:03:02.315 --> 00:03:03.082
However,

00:03:03.082 --> 00:03:04.284
I don't want to use the fact

00:03:04.284 --> 00:03:05.552
that he's exaggerating

00:03:05.552 --> 00:03:06.920
to not get at the fact that Mr..

00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:07.320
You're right.

00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:07.987
The IG, Mr.

00:03:07.987 --> 00:03:09.822
Horowitz, did find a lot of this, too.

00:03:09.822 --> 00:03:11.824
But these are some very important issues

00:03:11.824 --> 00:03:12.358
that Chris Wray,

00:03:12.358 --> 00:03:13.660
the FBI director, acknowledged,

00:03:13.660 --> 00:03:14.961
saying We've put a lot of reforms

00:03:14.961 --> 00:03:16.296
in place already.

00:03:16.296 --> 00:03:17.263
Because of these problems.

00:03:17.263 --> 00:03:18.331
Look, I will be the first

00:03:18.331 --> 00:03:19.265
to tell you, having worked

00:03:19.265 --> 00:03:19.999
at the Justice Department

00:03:19.999 --> 00:03:23.736
for six years, that if there is bias or

00:03:23.770 --> 00:03:25.605
the use of uncorroborated information

00:03:25.605 --> 00:03:26.072
in evidence

00:03:26.072 --> 00:03:27.540
it should be dealt with appropriately.

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:28.274
The simple fact is

00:03:28.274 --> 00:03:29.609
there are plenty of rules

00:03:29.609 --> 00:03:30.710
at both the judge department

00:03:30.710 --> 00:03:32.812
and the FBI for getting out

00:03:32.812 --> 00:03:34.080
political bias and

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:35.582
and predisposition to things

00:03:35.582 --> 00:03:36.816
to the point about predisposition.

00:03:36.816 --> 00:03:38.251
It's an important one.

00:03:38.251 --> 00:03:40.019
Everybody has a predisposition

00:03:40.019 --> 00:03:40.820
in some way.

00:03:40.820 --> 00:03:42.322
John, the question is,

00:03:42.322 --> 00:03:44.891
does it affect the work? And if it does.

00:03:45.091 --> 00:03:46.259
How do you deal with it

00:03:46.259 --> 00:03:47.227
on the back end now?

00:03:47.227 --> 00:03:48.795
Look, you can change the rules

00:03:48.795 --> 00:03:49.762
to make them different,

00:03:49.762 --> 00:03:50.330
then propose

00:03:50.330 --> 00:03:51.698
any of those such things here.

00:03:51.698 --> 00:03:52.599
You can prosecute

00:03:52.599 --> 00:03:53.733
people who broke the law.

00:03:53.733 --> 00:03:54.434
But look,

00:03:54.434 --> 00:03:56.636
they tried to bring three prosecutions.

00:03:56.636 --> 00:03:58.504
Two of them ended up going to trial

00:03:58.504 --> 00:03:59.472
and not guilty.

00:03:59.472 --> 00:04:01.374
One of them ended up

00:04:01.374 --> 00:04:03.643
pleading out for only probation.

00:04:03.643 --> 00:04:05.211
There simply wasn't

00:04:05.211 --> 00:04:07.180
the widespread problems

00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:08.548
that certainly the former president,

00:04:08.548 --> 00:04:09.582
the former attorney general

00:04:09.582 --> 00:04:11.651
wanted to find here and simply did not.

00:04:11.651 --> 00:04:14.487
And I mean, look, here we are in 20, 23.

00:04:14.487 --> 00:04:15.455
And I know a lot of people

00:04:15.455 --> 00:04:17.790
are really tired of talking about 20, 20.

00:04:18.091 --> 00:04:20.560
So here we go. We're talking about 2016.

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:21.861
And this is what this report is.

00:04:21.861 --> 00:04:23.963
It's kind of a little bit of a

00:04:23.963 --> 00:04:25.665
like you know,

00:04:25.665 --> 00:04:27.100
something like a message in a bottle

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:28.401
right from 2016.

00:04:28.401 --> 00:04:29.636
But it led to a special counsel

00:04:29.636 --> 00:04:31.170
investigation, led to an impeachment,

00:04:31.170 --> 00:04:32.105
which is why this is

00:04:32.105 --> 00:04:32.939
sometimes something

00:04:32.939 --> 00:04:35.208
worth revisiting history. Don't make.

00:04:35.208 --> 00:04:37.410
Durham goes out of his way to to to

00:04:37.577 --> 00:04:38.478
actually say that

00:04:38.478 --> 00:04:40.446
what Mueller found was very important

00:04:40.446 --> 00:04:41.981
and he seems to believe that

00:04:41.981 --> 00:04:43.983
what Mueller did was was legitimate

00:04:44.150 --> 00:04:45.351
But and so another point in

00:04:45.351 --> 00:04:46.252
this is his show

00:04:46.252 --> 00:04:47.186
the headline of the story

00:04:47.186 --> 00:04:47.687
you wrote about this.

00:04:47.687 --> 00:04:49.222
Durham interviewed Hillary Clinton

00:04:49.222 --> 00:04:50.456
on an alleged plan to tie Trump

00:04:50.456 --> 00:04:52.058
to Russia, found no provable

00:04:52.058 --> 00:04:54.027
criminal offense. What does that mean?

00:04:54.027 --> 00:04:55.561
It means that in the end,

00:04:55.561 --> 00:04:56.729
the government officials

00:04:56.729 --> 00:04:57.397
who were handling

00:04:57.397 --> 00:04:59.299
this did not commit a crime.

00:04:59.299 --> 00:05:00.900
You know, they were made mistakes

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:02.502
and they should have looked at this

00:05:02.502 --> 00:05:04.137
and maybe had second thoughts

00:05:04.137 --> 00:05:05.438
about what they were doing with Trump.

00:05:05.438 --> 00:05:06.105
And they didn't.

00:05:06.105 --> 00:05:07.173
And that's what he found.

00:05:07.173 --> 00:05:08.608
He recommends Durham

00:05:08.608 --> 00:05:09.042
like a not

00:05:09.042 --> 00:05:10.076
what I would call an ombudsman.

00:05:10.076 --> 00:05:11.044
That's why we call it the news business.

00:05:11.044 --> 00:05:11.611
Somebody

00:05:11.611 --> 00:05:12.312
if there's a politically

00:05:12.312 --> 00:05:13.212
sensitive investigation,

00:05:13.212 --> 00:05:13.980
someone who's not involved

00:05:13.980 --> 00:05:15.081
to be there to question

00:05:15.081 --> 00:05:15.648
just a question,

00:05:15.648 --> 00:05:16.316
everything along the way,

00:05:16.316 --> 00:05:17.250
there are things that will happen

00:05:17.250 --> 00:05:17.917
already.

00:05:17.917 --> 00:05:18.451
What they've done

00:05:18.451 --> 00:05:19.652
is that they've made sure

00:05:19.652 --> 00:05:20.219
there's more

00:05:20.219 --> 00:05:21.921
approvals needed for types

00:05:21.921 --> 00:05:23.423
of these types of investigations.

00:05:23.423 --> 00:05:24.357
We'll watch as it plays out.

00:05:24.357 --> 00:05:25.024
Gentlemen, thank you both.

